{
  "design_defect": "The assigned native_route fixes the join structure to exactly users -> message_reactions -> messages (r0,r1,r2) with no channels node. The selection condition requires that the reacted-to message be 'posted in #finance', which is only expressible via the channels table (channel_name) or by hardcoding the channel's internal ID on messages.channel_id — the latter uses a target-scoping ID rather than a visible identifying value, and the former requires extending the locked route with an additional table/join, which validation rejected as changing the assigned route. Since the selector was already locked after the first submission, no further revision to it is permitted, and no selector that both (a) preserves the exact locked route/joins and (b) faithfully encodes the #finance channel condition without using a target-identifying scope can be constructed. This is a genuine conflict between the fixed native route and the stated selection conditions, not a compilation error I can silently repair."
}
